  "description": "Data is split into addressed packets that take different routes and are reassembled on arrival. Between continents almost all traffic (~99%) travels through undersea fiber-optic cables, over 1.4 million km of them, where data moves as pulses of light. In deep water many cables are about as thin as a garden hose, and the odd shark has bitten one. Original 3D animation.",
